{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_8e50267e5249f49e19f04ff7030ef271f0bd1badb1717d56602da340ffb6e5bd"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README describes the stack as TypeScript/Electron.js, a Next.js/React landing page with Supabase auth, a Python Flask backend with Supabase, and Axiom for logging/telemetry."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a70c1e2c74e33f0f932c0ae0f4e78fc455c549572bc3c787ceb54af9821353ea"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README states Pear has context on the user's codebase so questions can be asked directly, with code stored locally on the user's computer."},{"claim_ids":["clm_de27e3248cf88433671c69a714bfb843a13285e705cab6fae735f71217e6a0c3"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Because PearAI is a VSCode fork, the README claims users get a familiar editor experience and can pick up where they left off."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f2cdd0c1f4886c125399e31b1a26c14f76e4c235b42da66b4f9276adecb1ee77"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README states Pear OSS is Apache 2.0 licensed, but the included LICENSE.txt is Microsoft's MIT license, suggesting inherited VSCode code remains under MIT alongside the project license claim."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f8e5a885886312803a492bbfab56a252e0f09dd95c12a5abeb2fa80adebd5417"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"PearAI is described as a fork of VSCode, with its main functionality in a separate submodule (pearai-submodule) that is itself a fork of Continue."}],"claim_ids":["clm_8e50267e5249f49e19f04ff7030ef271f0bd1badb1717d56602da340ffb6e5bd","clm_a70c1e2c74e33f0f932c0ae0f4e78fc455c549572bc3c787ceb54af9821353ea","clm_de27e3248cf88433671c69a714bfb843a13285e705cab6fae735f71217e6a0c3","clm_f2cdd0c1f4886c125399e31b1a26c14f76e4c235b42da66b4f9276adecb1ee77","clm_f8e5a885886312803a492bbfab56a252e0f09dd95c12a5abeb2fa80adebd5417"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:20:38Z","created_by_operation":"op_befb270798e64c25b18cd871916efc48","id":"pg_63a0f7b29827547781220e8c9a041d63","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages